\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Safe home, safe home in port!
\par Rent cordage, shattered deck,
\par Torn  sails, provision short,
\par And only not a wreck;
\par But O the joy upon the shore
\par To tell the voyage- perils o'er!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The prize, the prize secure!
\par The athlete nearly fell;
\par Bare all he could endure,
\par And bare not always well:
\par But he may smile at troubles gone
\par Who sets the victor- garland on.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. No more the foe can harm:
\par No more of leaguered camp,
\par And cry of night alarm,
\par And need of ready lamp:
\par And yet how nearly had he failed,
\par How nearly had that foe prevailed!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The exile is at home:
\par O nights and days of tears
\par O longings not to roam!
\par O sins, and doubts, and fears!
\par What matters now grief's darkest day?
\par The King has wiped those tears away.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

